# Chain Management

## Home Chain (Secret Network)
- Primary responsibility: Signature completion (Round 7 MPC)
- Contract queries for:
  - User entry code hash
  - Public keys (secp256k1, ed25519)
- Does NOT handle:
  - Wallet backup/recovery
  - Key metadata management
  - MPC signing coordination

## Target Chains
- Supports multiple blockchain types:
  - Cosmos chains (CosmosChainId)
  - Secret Network (SecretChainId)
  - EVM chains (Eip155ChainId)
  - Solana (SolanaChainId)
- Chain-specific adapters with unified interfaces
- IBC channel management for Cosmos chains
- Chain-specific transaction handling

# Client Application

## Core Responsibilities
- MPC signing coordination
- Key metadata management
- Wallet backup and recovery
- Chain-specific adapters
- Share encryption/decryption

## Signing Flow
1. Transaction Preparation (Client)
   - Hash calculation
   - Message serialization
   - Fee estimation

2. Pre-signing Phase (Client)
   - Easy Share used for partial signing
   - Partial signature generation
   - Client-side coordination

3. Final Signing
   - Secret Network smart contract query with network share
   - Secret Network replies with completed signature (final round of multi-party computation)
   - Transaction broadcast to target network (can be EVM, Cosmos, Bitcoin. Solana is supported but not with MPC signing - it uses a local key for now.)

# Backup System

## Backup Content
- Wallet data and user information
- Encrypted shares (Easy Share and Backup Share)
- Key metadata and configuration
- Ed25519 key pair (when present)
- Owner configuration (threshold and keys)

## Encryption Model
- Threshold-based encryption (N of M keys)
- MultisigKeyEncryption for backup data
- SharesEncryptionForClient for client data
- Standardized encoding patterns

## Health Monitoring
- Backup availability checks
- Easy Share verification
- Data synchronization validation
- Version control through revisions

## Storage Architecture
- Worker-based API for management
- Legacy data migration support
- Secure retrieval protocols

# Encoding Patterns

## Standardized Classes
- Base64EncodedString
- HexEncodedString
- Base58EncodedString (Solana)
- Utf8EncodedString

## Utility Methods
- fromBase64/toBase64
- fromHex/toHex
- fromBytes/toBytes
- Proper padding handling

## Schema Validation
- Zod for runtime type safety
- Common schema patterns:
  - Transaction validation
  - Wallet data validation
  - User input validation
  - API response validation
- Custom transformers and validators

